   <text type="letter">
      <body>
         <div type="writingSession">
            <pb n="1"/>
            <opener><dateline>99 Claremont-Avenue, New York City<date when="1936-01-27">27. Jan
                     36</date></dateline>
               <salute>Dear <rs type="person"><!-- Person muss noch angelegt werden--> Mr
                     Brightman</rs>:</salute>
            </opener>
            <p>I feel extremely guilty that I did not answer your very kind <rs ref="L10243">letter</rs> from <date when="1935-12-01">Dez. 1.</date>
               earlier. There were two reasons for that. First because I did not want to answer
               without a rather large explanation of my ideas concerning the idea of God and that I
               did not find any time for doing so in the last two months, because I to prepare the
               publication of an own book of mine. Second because the difficulty of writing in
               Englisch, which hampers me not so much in lecturing as in the attempts to express as
               subtlime ideas as are implied in your proposed <unclear reason="illegible"
                  >¿¿¿</unclear>. Now I want to tell you that I shall be in <!-- place id muss ergänzt werden-->
               <rs ref="#tillich_place_id__1" type="place">Cambridge</rs> about 4 or 5 days between
               the <date when="1936-02-11">11th</date> and the <date when="1936-02-16">16th</date> of February. In these days I think we should have a great
               discussion concerning our common problems. I hope you will be able to give this time,
               and most of all, I hope you pardon me for the terrible delay of my answer. It occured
               as it usually does: <unclear reason="illegible">¿¿¿</unclear> I did not want to give
               a short answer I did not answer at all. In every case i will try to call you as soon
               as I have arrived in Boston.</p>
            <closer><salute>Very cordially yours</salute>
               <signed><rs ref="#tillich_person_id__1928" type="person">Paul J. Tillich</rs>
               </signed></closer>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
